    "narrative": "For today's matchup, **Junior Caminero** and **Christian Yelich** headline our lineup, both delivering high-floor utility. **Junior Caminero** earns the day's highest score (71.46) by leveraging a favorable matchup against Tanner Bibee, bolstered by a significant SP skill advantage. Meanwhile, **Christian Yelich** (74.33) is our strongest overall play; while he faces Ryan Feltner, his dynamic platoon advantage as a left-handed hitter against a righty, combined with a lead-off spot, makes him an elite start despite the park factors. **Colt Keith** (69.64) and **Yordan Alvarez** (66.90) round out our core; **Colt Keith** benefits from a rare combination of leadoff usage and an SP skill edge against Wacha, while **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start due to his elite xwOBA, which continues to anchor our offense regardless of the matchup against Sean Burke.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of our \"Lineup Pending\" status, particularly regarding **Trea Turner** and **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (60.33) is a strong start due to his stolen base upside, he faces a daunting matchup against Paul Skenes, an elite arm that heavily pressures his projection. Similarly, **Trea Turner** (57.37) sees a score reduction due to the elite holding capability of Ryan Weathers, which tempers his stolen base expectations significantly. **Lars Nootbaar** was our most difficult cut from the starting nine; his 43.93 score remained competitive, but he fell just short of the efficiency threshold due to the unfavorable matchup against Hunter Greene\u2019s high-velocity profile, which ultimately favored the higher-upside profiles of our active OF rotation. We are monitoring all lineups closely, as any shift in the batting order for **Gary Sanchez** or **Chase Meidroth** could force a late-afternoon recalibration of our efficiency targets.",
